SO-101 robot model and meshes

soarm/robot/so101.xml and all 19 STL meshes in soarm/robot/assets/ are
copied from MuJoCo Menagerie, robotstudio_so101,
commit ac6b2b09983786f3036cab1000221017fa2193b4:
https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie/tree/ac6b2b09983786f3036cab1000221017fa2193b4/robotstudio_so101

The meshes are unmodified. Machinekind modified so101.xml: the solver runs
20 iterations (was 10) and 50 line search iterations (was 20), and the
gripper's contact geoms use solimp 0.9 0.995 0.001 (was MuJoCo's default).
The file carries a notice of the change.

The upstream README credits The Robot Studio SO101 robot and includes
the attribution "developed by I2RT Robotics".

Menagerie derives the model from TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100. Its README
identifies aec17bbc256d1a7342d53aaa4950595d4c30b40d as the copied XML
version and links to the original MJCF at 608122e9ac330a753735f2e18aee73338e9ac407:
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/aec17bbc256d1a7342d53aaa4950595d4c30b40d/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.xml
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/blob/608122e9ac330a753735f2e18aee73338e9ac407/Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.xml

