tools/graspgenx/so101/gripper.urdf (in the repository, not in this package)
is derived from soarm/robot/so101.xml above: the gripper subtree rewritten
by hand as URDF for GraspGenX, the wrist camera mount and the primitive
collision geoms left out. It references the same meshes and carries the
same Apache-2.0 license; the file identifies itself as modified in its
header, as Apache-2.0 section 4 asks.

Overhead camera mount

soarm/robot/fixtures/overhead_cam_32/cam_mount_bottom.stl, cam_mount_middle.stl
and cam_mount_top.stl are derived from TheRobotStudio's SO-ARM100 "Overhead
Camera w/ 32x32 Camera Module", stl/ at commit
c8af7c4b7abe191b149c618bb36044425f4ad159:
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/tree/c8af7c4b7abe191b149c618bb36044425f4ad159/Optional/Overhead_Cam_Mount_32x32_UVC_Module

Machinekind modified them: scaled from millimetres to metres and moved into
each part's own frame (z up). Each file's header says so. fixture.yaml (the
colliders, the part stack, the camera site and the placements beside the
SO-101) is Machinekind's, written by tools/overhead_cam_mount.py (in the
repository, not in this package) from those files and the design's
arm_base.stl, which is not included.

